<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Appendix</h2>

<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Detail of LongBench</h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we present the metric of each subset of the different chunking methods on LongBench, and the results are shown in <a href="#A1.T1" title="Table A1 ‣ A.1 Detail of LongBench ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ HiChunk: Evaluating and Enhancing Retrieval-Augmented Generation with Hierarchical Chunking" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table A1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.T1" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A1.T1.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table A1</span>: </span><span id="A1.T1.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">RAG-pipeline evaluation on LongBench and each subset. The best result is in <span id="A1.T1.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">bold</span>, and the sub-optimal result is in <span id="A1.T1.6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_underline">underlined</span>. Qasper* is the subset of LongBench.</span></figcaption>
<div id="A1.T1.7" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:310.5pt;height:138.5pt;vertical-align:-67.8pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-117.3pt,52.3pt) scale(0.569543189404803,0.569543189404803) ;">
